@host = http://localhost:5099

### Health
GET {{host}}/health

### List all users (public)
# @name list
GET {{host}}/api/users

### Create a user — 201
# @name create
POST {{host}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ada Lovelace",
  "age": 36,
  "city": "London",
  "state": "Greater London",
  "pincode": "WC1E"
}

### Create with every field invalid — 400 with a per-field `errors` dictionary
POST {{host}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "A",
  "age": 999,
  "city": "",
  "state": "",
  "pincode": "1"
}

### Get one by id (public)
GET {{host}}/api/users/{{create.response.body.id}}

### Get an unknown id — 404
GET {{host}}/api/users/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Replace a user
PUT {{host}}/api/users/{{create.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Grace Hopper",
  "age": 45,
  "city": "Arlington",
  "state": "VA",
  "pincode": "22201"
}

### Delete a user — 204, then 404 on a repeat
DELETE {{host}}/api/users/{{create.response.body.id}}

### With Auth:Enabled=true, writes need a bearer token (reads stay public)
POST {{host}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <paste-an-access-token>

{
  "name": "Katherine Johnson",
  "age": 40,
  "city": "Hampton",
  "state": "VA",
  "pincode": "23666"
}
